            <ArticleTitle>[Right ventricular outflow obstruction due to a giant pseudoaneurysm of the anterior descending coronary artery in a patient with Behçet's disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>297-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Giant pseudoaneurysms of coronary arteries in patients with Behçet's disease is a uncommon finding. It has been described exceptionally in the literature. We present a case of giant pseudoaneurysm of the left anterior descending coronary artery with obstruction of the right ventricular outflow in a patient with Behçet's disease. He improved after surgical resection and steroid treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
